export anchor SonarStyle:
    number: 303
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Sonar
    idea: A submarine sonar console in deep sea green, where a round scope with a sweeping arc plots the twelve checks as contacts, the failing one pinged and labelled, and rounded instrument bezels hold the rest.
    base: dark
    palette:
        abyss: #021411, the page, style sheet ground, fields and dials
        console: #06211b, the header strip, tabs and console gradient base
        consoleTop: #0a2c24, console gradient tops and the comment
        bezel: #14453a, instrument rims and chips
        grid: #1a4b3f, dividers and scope rings
        ink: #d2f8e8, text
        kelp: #86c7ad, labels, bearings and meta
        sonarGreen: #3ff0a2, the sweep, contacts, passed, approved, added lines, the current tab, the primary button and focus
        amber: #ffc862, changes requested, the ping comment and Private
        coral: #ff8b7b, the failing contact and removed lines
        coralShade: #2e1716, the failing row and removed line ground
    type:
        A wide humanist sans, Tahoma, Verdana, DejaVu Sans, for headings at
        700, the title at 26px and figures at 26px in sonar green. Verdana
        for text at 13.5px and 1.55 and labels at 10.5px bold caps tracked
        0.14em. Data and the diff use Lucida Sans Typewriter or a system
        monospace at 11.5 to 12.5px.
    layout:
        A pill shaped header strip holds a round badge with a green ring,
        Brightwork Code and the repository, an amber Private label and pill
        counters, with rounded tabs below and the current one filled
        green. The upper band has two instruments. The scope bezel holds a
        round sonar display with three rings, crosshairs, bearings 000 to
        270, a green sweep wedge and a bright sweep line, and twelve
        contacts as green dots, the seventh a coral ringed cross with a
        dashed ping ring and the label 07 e2e-android. Beside it a contact
        list numbers every check with a tick, the failing row tinted
        coral, and under it 11 of 12 checks passed and the failing line.
        The contact report bezel holds the Open pill, the title, the merge
        sentence, two rounded reviewer dials, and a waterfall of the three
        files, each with counts and a dotted green trail scaled to its
        additions. The lower band holds the signal log with the diff,
        where the comment is a Ping bubble with an amber rim and a glowing
        ring marker, and a details bezel with assignee, pill labels,
        milestone, linked issue and a dashed disabled merge. Below 1100px
        the bands stack, below 700px the contact list wraps in two columns.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between instruments, 18px inside bezels, 12px between dials.
    density: Medium. A large scope beside the contact report, then a wide signal log.
    corners: Round. 20px bezels, 14px dials, a pill header, a circular scope and pill chips.
    borders: 2px bezel rims with a 4px dark inner rim, 1px grid lines, a 2px amber rim on the comment.
    shadows: Soft drop shadows under bezels and a glow ring on the ping marker.
    icons:
        1.9px line icons. Dots for passed contacts and a ringed cross for
        the failing one on the scope, and in lists a tick, an octagon cross,
        a ringed tick and a triangle, each with its word.
    focus: A 2px sonar green outline offset 3px with a soft green halo.
    tone: Calm sonar words, such as Scope, Contact report, Waterfall, Signal log, Ping and Holding depth until all checks pass.
